Theory: C_α is a torsor under E_Hm, so Jac(C_α) is isomorphic to E_Hm (over Q-bar).
However, the J-invariant is preserved, so j(Jac(C_α)) = j(E_Hm) always.
Conductors should equal N(E_Hm) (up to local twist).

Useful fact: if Jac(C_α) is Q-isomorphic to E_Hm, then ellrank(J(C_α)) = ellrank(E_Hm).
Twist analysis: J(C_α) is a 2-isogenous quadratic twist of E_Hm.
